# Context

## Why This Way
Mid-run finding: on the crossdevice question the ohya-arm model tried
`ls` twice to check whether the ohya repo exists locally, both attempts
were denied by the allowlist sandbox, and it then answered correctly
through sql alone. The old audit condemned the run as invalid on the
attempt alone. Cross-access must mean successful execution, and the
result event's permission_denials (tool_use_id) is the authoritative
signal. regrade exists because grading evolves independently of the
expensive client runs.

## Gotchas
- stream-json tool_result blocks carry no id; only the result event's
  permission_denials pairs denials back to tool_use ids.
- Keep timeout and error verdicts untouched in regrade: they describe
  run conditions that a re-parse cannot re-derive.
